The solution to the problem involves using a workaround that leverages the fact that even though the constructors are internal, the class itself is public. This approach involves creating a public static method within a helper class that acts as a wrapper around the desired constructor. This method can then be invoked using Reflection, as shown below:

```csharp
public static class ClassNameHelper
{
    public static ClassName CreateInstance(double value, bool flag)
    {
        // Use Reflection to invoke the internal constructor
        var constructors = typeof(ClassName).GetConstructors();
        foreach (var ctor in constructors)
        {
            if (ctor.IsInternal)
            {
                // Find the parameter names corresponding to the given arguments
                var parameters = ctor.GetParameters();
                var parameterIndex = parameters.IndexOfParameter(value.GetType());
                if (parameterIndex != -1)
                {
                    ctor.Invoke(new object[] { value, flag });
                    return (ClassName)ctor.Invoke(null);
                }
            }
        }
        // Handle the case where no matching constructor is found
        throw new ArgumentException("No matching constructor found for the given arguments.");
    }
}

// Usage
var instance = ClassNameHelper.CreateInstance(42.0, true);
